WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.334
Child welfare crisis.

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:05.329
The youngest victims of institutional failure.

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:12.863
Indigenous children are overrepresented in the child welfare system at rates that the Canadian Human Rights Tribunal has ruled discriminatory.

00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:25.034
Jordan's Principle — the legal obligation to provide First Nations children with services comparable to other children — has required repeated tribunal orders to enforce, and the government has been found in non-compliance multiple times.

00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:28.806
One in four Canadian children experience food insecurity.

00:00:28.806 --> 00:00:32.090
The disability benefit for children is inadequate.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.102
Childcare waitlists persist despite the ten-dollar-a-day program.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:41.113
The institutional failures documented across this site do not only harm adults.

00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:48.068
They harm the most vulnerable Canadians of all — children who cannot advocate for themselves, vote, or file ATIP requests.

00:00:48.068 --> 00:00:51.204
Three documented child welfare failures.
